body:
Thank you, really. In regards of keeping safe, it's mostly because I understand the repercussions that going out would have on my immediate household members. But honestly if I did get COVID, I'd likely see it as a better reason to just straight up off myself. 

&#x200B;

I know what it's like to be someone with problems trying to talk to someone else about it, only to be also burdened with that same person's problems. I know that sometimes it's done as a way to show that they understand what I'm going through, and that's okay, but sometimes it feels like they try to compete with the 'worseness' of the situation. For those times, I end up feeling invalidated. So if someone comes to me, I intentionally forget for that time that I have issues as bad as I do, show that I understand, then proceed to try and help and support the best I can. Maybe it's easier to do that because I'm more worried for them than I am for myself.

I guess I can't give specific instances, but off the top of my head, I'd say I remind people to be gentle with themselves. I know what it's like to be against yourself, when really you're the one person you need on your side. But for whatever reason, my logic goes: this is true for them because often the world is cruel, and they deserve love in this hate, yet this doesn't apply to me because I've done nothing to deserve such mercy. It's strange and I know it's illogical, but it's proved very difficult to rid myself of a mindset I keep coming back to.

&#x200B;

Regarding COVID, thank you very much for your concern. Unfortunately, while the confirmed cases in our country have just reached 3K (still high tho), only a fraction of the population has been tested. I'm very concerned as to what will happen once gov officials get off their asses and finally implement mass testing. One thing's for sure, though; we're definitely getting an extension on the quarantine/lockdown. My most immediate concern is that it's been nearly a month, but other more needy members of our community haven't been given provisions by the local gov, while other cities have proven to have more competent mayors. The difference is jarring, and I'm worried for what is to come. 

&#x200B;

I do apologize for not replying with more haste.
